# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so everything
# .gitignore excluded has to be repeated here or it gets uploaded.
#
# The reason it exists: `ios/` is 1.2 GB of generated Xcode project and is not
# gitignored, so every build shipped it to the cloud. That made the tarball
# ~106 MB and the upload failed part-way with EPIPE. EAS runs `prebuild` and
# regenerates the native projects itself, and an Android build has no use for
# `ios/` at all.

# Generated native projects - EAS regenerates these
ios/
android/

# From .gitignore
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Local noise that has no business in a build
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage/
.git/
